From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:07:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ask_contact with no usable goal id finds its goal instead of
 failing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

14 first tries in three days were refused „Task not found or not open"
(tool_call_log, 11-14 Oct; the tester's 58029 run 2 and 0248's trios
among them). The owner typed „ask Gela ..." in a conversation with no
goal yet, the model called ask_contact with task_id 0, and a whole model
round went on create_task before the same ask went again.

With no usable id, the ask now takes this conversation's open goal. If
there is none and the owner's line is an instruction to ask someone, it
opens that goal itself, exactly as the server's own send already does
(goalForInstruction, 3928). Every other case keeps the same refusal. No
model-facing text changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
